<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12177" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cynosbătŏs</span></b> ,
			i, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυνόσβατος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The dog-rose</i> or <i>wild-brier</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 37, 71, § 179</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Col.
				11, 3, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App. Herb.
			87</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Cynosbatos, also called cynapanxis or neurospastos, <i>the black currant</i>: Ribes nigrum, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 24,
				14, 74, § 121</span></i>; also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cynospastos</span></b>  (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυνόσπαστος</span>), <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The caper - bush</i>: Capparis spinosa, Linn.;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				13, 23, 44, § 127</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
